  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Fri Jul 3 2026\n\nA hot and humid airmass will remain over the forecast area as we\ngo through the 4th of July weekend. While the recent heat stress \nis on the higher end of the normal range, values have trended \ndownward some, and this makes the current heat stress event a \nlittle more marginal. Given it is a holiday weekend with a peak \nin outdoor activities and gatherings, we're being a little more \naggressive with the messaging, and a heat advisory has been \nexpanded to include the entire area through the 4th. Thereafter, a\nmore definite weakness will develop in the subtropical ridge, and\nthis will support greater coverage of convective rainfall \ncoverage with earlier onset in the diurnal cycle. Because of this,\npeak heat indices and duration become a little more questionable \nin terms of meeting heat advisory thresholds, so will hold off on\ngoing further out. Overall, a typical active July convective \nregime is expected along with seasonably hot and humid conditions\nas we end the weekend and go through early to mid next week. \nAdditional heat related graphics for limited/elevated heat threats \nmay eventually become necessary as we get closer in time. /EC/",
